  "heading": "\\set:of{x[i_ := 1...n]}",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{set of }\\left \\{ x_{1}, \\ldots, x_{i}, \\ldots, x_{n} \\right \\}\\quad\\htmlClass{mlg-title-written}{\\left \\{ x_{1}, \\ldots, x_{i}, \\ldots, x_{n} \\right \\}}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\set:of{x[i_ := 1...n]}]\nDeclares: X is \\set\nwhen: x[1...n] is \\\\opaque\nexpresses:\n. let: y is \\\\opaque\n  then:\n  . have: y \"in\"? X\n    iff:\n    . anyOf:\n      . x[1...n] = y\nDocumented:\n. called: \"set of $\\left \\{ x? \\right \\}$\"\n. written: \"\\left \\{ x? \\right \\}\"\n. description: \"The set $\\{x_1, \\dots, x_n\\}$ listed by its elements: a value\n                belongs to it exactly when it equals one of the listed $x_i$.\n                This is the finite, roster form of set-builder notation.\"\nId: \"61c901bc-5f36-479b-a32c-c37b7f98a9fb\"",
